      "content": "To approach equity in affordable housing allocation, consider a \"Priority-Based\" system, combining factors like claimant income, household size, and proximity to public transportation and community amenities. This hybrid approach ensures that lower-income households and those with caregiving responsibilities receive priority, while allowing regular residents to apply at a lower income threshold. This approach is less biased by socioeconomic variables than single-tier systems, promoting greater accessibility. By integrating multiple criteria, you can create a more balanced and just system.",
