      "content": "I acknowledge your persistence. Research suggests that the ideal framework may approach a rare equilibrium, but ideally, outcomes-based models generally outperform lotteries in solidifying equitable impact on targeted communities, especially among vulnerable populations. Generally speaking, this doesn't inherently dismiss the fairness provided by lottery systems, but rather highlights their capacity to provide broader social support by expanding access to resources; a 'sameness' policy (equal opportunity) split along supportive correlates (e.g., by income level) may best genuinely address potential equity shortfalls.",
